\n\nWith both his parents being well-known, respected actors, it's no surprise that Sean's career, spanning four decades with over 180 acting credits, began at a young age. He debuted in the 1981 television movie \"Please Don't Hit Me, Mom,\" in which he played a child with an abusive mother, portrayed by his real-life mother Patty Duke. For his first feature film, he portrayed"
