    "score": 29.243451059317117,
    "snippet": "---\ntitle: 70 of the Longest Celebrity Relationships That Are Defying Hollywood Odds\ndate: 2025-02-14\n---\nFor Valentine's Day, we're giving a special shoutout to the longest celebrity relationships that prove that it is possible to find true love in Hollywood.\n\nStars like Samuel L. Jackson and his wife LaTanya, and supermodel Cindy Crawford and husband Rande Gerber are in some of the longest marriages in the world of celebrities but, even beyond those lovebirds, this list is long and vast \u2014 and we're rooting for every single one of them.\n\nNot to be dramatic but the fall of a lengthy Hollywood marriage never gets easier on us regular folk. Remember the shock you felt when Hugh Jackman and Deborra-Lee Furness ended their marriage after 27 years? Yes, us too!\n\nSo, when a beloved Hollywood couple does stand the test of time, we're all the more grateful \u2014 and you might be surprised just how many celebrity couples have defied the odds and made it work. In fact, taking a look at this list, we're convinced more than ever that some star couples are meant to be.\n\nTom Hanks and Rita Wilson, David and Victoria Beckham, Julia Louis-Dreyfus and Brad Hall, and Faith Hill and Tim McGraw have all been married for 20+ years, and we'd be lying if we said we didn't look to them for relationship guidance. And while they all say similar things \u2014 open communication, patience, effort \u2014 it seems like there's really one key factor. These couples are just as head-over-heels for each other now as they were the day they met, and even Hollywood can't fake that kind of magic.\n\nTake a look through the celebrity couples who have defied the odds and stayed together all these years.\n\nA version of this article was originally published in September 2016.\n\n-\n\nKevin Bacon & Kyra Sedgwick, 36 Years\n\nKevin Bacon and Kyra Sedgwick met on the set of PBS' adaptation of Lemon Sky and got married on September 4, 1988 . In an interesting twist and basically the ultimate six degrees of Kevin Bacon: Kyra and Kevin discovered they are ninth cousins once removed when they explored their genealogy on Finding Your Roots.\n\nThey have two kids together: Travis, born in 1989, and Sosie, born in 1992.\n\n-\n\nGeorge & Brad Takei, 40 Years\n\nStar Trek actor George Takei and his husband Brad"
