    "snippet": "---\ntitle: The 15 youngest Oscar winners and nominees of all time\ndate: 2024-03-10\n---\nThe 15 youngest Oscar winners and nominees of all time\n\nHistory is being teased at Oscars 2021, as an unprecedented number of performers of color are nominated for amazing work in all four top acting categories.\n\nThe late Chadwick Boseman is up for Best Actor with his final role as hot-headed musician Levee in Netflix's \"Ma Rainey's Black Bottom,\" which also scored his leading lady, Viola Davis, a nomination for Best Actress.\n\nSteven Yeun already made Oscars history, becoming the first Asian-American ever nominated for Best Actor for his role in \"Minari.\"\n\nDaniel Kaluuya and LaKeith Stanfield will face off in the same category, with both nominated for Best Actor in a Supporting Role in \"Judas and the Black Messiah.\"\n\nMeanwhile, \"Minari\" star Youn Yuh-jung is up for Best Actress in a Supporting Role for a scene-stealing performance that's already nabbed her several top critics' prizes.\n\nWill these actors break new cinematic ground at Oscars 2021?\n\nThese and other grown-up questions will be answered when the 93rd annual Academy Awards ceremony \u2014 broadcast live from the Dolby Theatre in Hollywood, Calif. \u2014 airs at 8 p.m. Sunday, April 25, on ABC. That's when Hollywood's institution will attempt to break the \"Zoom curse\" of plummeting awards show ratings amid the ongoing COVID-19 pandemic.\n\nUntil then, let's take a look back at the youngest talents to be considered for Tinseltown's most prestigious awards competition.\n\nSure, the adorable Alan Kim was snubbed by Oscar for his acclaimed work in \"Minari\" \u2014 even after his heart-tugging, tear-jerking win at the Critics' Choice Awards went mega-viral.\n\nBut at 8 years old, Kim still has plenty of time to join the greats: From little Jackie Cooper in 1931's cute \"Skippy\" to Quvenzhan\u00e9 Wallis in 2013's haunting \"Beasts of the Southern Wild,\" here is a rundown of the most youthful performers to strike gold \u2014 or close to it.\n\nAnd the youngest Oscar winners are \u2026\n\nTatum O'Neal: Best Supporting Actress 1974\n\nAt 10 years old, O'Neal became the youngest winner ever in a competitive category for her whiskey-voiced turn as Addie Pray, a pint-sized con artist selling"
