    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Top 10 successful Kenyan actors in Hollywood 2020\nauthor: Caiaphas Wanjala\ndate: 2020-12-25\n---\nTop 10 successful Kenyan actors in Hollywood 2020\n\nWho is the best actor in Kenya? With each dawn, more and more African actors and actresses are getting featured and earning a spotlight in Hollywood's biggest movie and film industry. That said, several successful Kenyan actors in Hollywood have made a name for themselves due to their acting prowess.\n\nThe Kenyan actors and actresses in Hollywood fly the 254 flag very high and put the country on the world map. There are outstanding Kenyan actors and actresses whose accomplishments are a big inspiration for many to pursue their interests regardless of their backgrounds.\n\nTop 10 successful Kenyan actors in Hollywood\n\nWho are the top 10 most famous actors? Since Hollywood is the biggest home to prominent television and movie production companies globally, it goes without saying that the Kenyans working in the industry earn hefty salaries. Here are the famous Kenyan actors in Hollywood.\n\n1. Edi Gathegi\n\nEdi Mue Gathegi is probably one of the Kenyan actors with the most features in Hollywood movies. For this reason, he tops this list as one of the most talented and highly paid Kenyan actors in Hollywood.\n\nEdi was born in Kenya on March 10th, 1979, and at three years old, his family relocated to California, USA. Acting was not on his radar as Gathegi was to pursue basketball at the University of California. However, due to a knee injury, his plans changed, and he decided to study acting at New York University.\n\nEdi's first film role was playing Haitian Cabbie in the film Crank (2006). Ever since then, Edi Gathegi has been cast for several celebrated movies and television series, including The Blacklist, StartUp, Twilight, Veronica Mars, Into the Badlands, The Blacklist: Redemption, Lincoln Heights, Nikita, CSI: Miami, and X Men: First Class.\n\n2. Lupita Nyong'o\n\nWithout a doubt, Lupita Nyong'o is one of the renowned Kenyan actors and actresses doing big things in Hollywood. She was born in Mexico but grew up in Kenya; therefore, she possesses dual citizenship. Her father is a well-known politician, Professor Anyang' Nyong'o, who is the reigning governor of Kisumu County. Ms Nyong'o is the second"
